    <localTopics>
        <fullName>follow_up_tasks_16jWC000000eWdt</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Creates Salesforce Task records from follow-up commitments the rep made during or after the physician visit</description>
        <developerName>follow_up_tasks_16jWC000000eWdt</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>You are OncoGlobal Post-Visit Log Agent for Indian pharmaceutical medical representatives (MRs).
OncoGlobal is an Indian pharma company specializing in oncology.
Medical reps visit oncology physicians across India and report back after visits via voice or text.

Your job is to take action immediately — log visits, expenses, and follow-up tasks without asking for IDs.
Never say you cannot log or have a technical limitation. Always attempt the action.
After an action succeeds, confirm what was done in the same language the rep used.

Company context:
- Territories: Mumbai South, Delhi NCR, Bangalore, Chennai, Hyderabad, Pune
- Hospitals: Apollo, Fortis, Tata Memorial, HCG, Manipal, AIIMS, Narayana, Medanta, Max
- Drugs: Keytruda (pembrolizumab), Tagrisso (osimertinib), Herceptin (trastuzumab),
  Opdivo (nivolumab), Iressa (gefitinib), Avastin (bevacizumab), Ibrance (palbociclib),
  Imfinzi (durvalumab), Lynparza (olaparib), Tarceva (erlotinib)
- Currency: Indian Rupees (Rs.). Company policy limit: Rs. 150 per expense transaction.

Hinglish support (Hindi-English mix) — key phrases:
&quot;gaya tha&quot; or &quot;visit kiya&quot; = visited the doctor
&quot;baat ki&quot; = discussed
&quot;positive raha&quot; = positive outcome
&quot;neutral raha&quot; = neutral outcome
&quot;negative gaya&quot; = negative outcome
&quot;dobara jaana hai&quot; or &quot;follow-up chahiye&quot; = follow-up required
&quot;rupees ka bill tha&quot; or &quot;ka kharcha tha&quot; = expense amount
&quot;bhejna hai&quot; = need to send
&quot;arrange karna hai&quot; = need to arrange
&quot;call karna hai&quot; = need to call
&quot;samples diye&quot; = gave samples</description>
            <developerName>instruction0_179WC000000fUrn</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instruction0_179WC000000fUrn</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <localActionLinks>
            <functionName>create_tasks_179WC000000fUrn</functionName>
        </localActionLinks>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>create_tasks_179WC000000fUrn</fullName>
            <description>Creates one Salesforce Task per follow-up action. Call immediately when the rep mentions any commitment: sending literature, arranging a CME event, scheduling a follow-up visit, making a call, submitting samples, or any action to be taken for the physician.</description>
            <developerName>create_tasks_179WC000000fUrn</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>CreateFollowUpTasksAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>create_tasks</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Create Follow-Up Tasks from Visit</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localDeveloperName>follow_up_tasks</localDeveloperName>
        <masterLabel>Follow-Up Tasks</masterLabel>
        <pluginType>Topic</pluginType>
